## 3. Commercial Use

The compiled Software may be used free of charge in commercial products.

You may distribute MPointCloud binaries as part of a larger commercial application, provided that:

1. MPointCloud is not sold or licensed as a standalone competing library;
2. MPointCloud remains identifiable as a third-party dependency or component;
3. the attribution requirements in this License are satisfied;
4. the distributed application does not claim authorship or ownership of MPointCloud;
5. copyright and license notices are preserved.

You may charge for your own application, service, product, platform, or solution that uses MPointCloud.

The fact that MPointCloud is included in a paid product does not transfer any ownership rights in MPointCloud to the distributor or end user.

## 4. Mandatory Attribution

Any product, application, service, package, or distribution that includes or depends upon MPointCloud must provide reasonable attribution to MPointCloud and its copyright holder.

Attribution must appear in at least one reasonably discoverable location accessible to the end user, customer, developer, or recipient, as appropriate to the type of product being distributed.

Acceptable locations include, but are not limited to:

- an About dialog or About page;
- a Help or Credits section;
- a Third-Party Software or Dependencies page;
- product documentation;
- dependency documentation;
- a NOTICE file;
- an acknowledgements file;
- a legal notices page;
- application package metadata;
- NuGet package metadata;
- software-bill-of-materials documentation;
- other locations where third-party dependency notices are normally presented.

The attribution should substantially identify:

**MPointCloud — high-performance .NET point-cloud data I/O library**  
**Copyright © 2026 Mekneo**

and should indicate that MPointCloud is used under the MPointCloud Free Binary License.

A hyperlink to the official MPointCloud repository, package, website, or project page may also be included where appropriate.

The attribution requirement does not require prominent advertising, splash-screen branding, or marketing placement.

The purpose of the attribution requirement is to preserve recognition of authorship and ownership and prevent MPointCloud from being represented as the original work or property of another person or organization.

## 5. No False Claim of Authorship or Ownership

You may not state, imply, advertise, document, or represent that you or your organization created, authored, invented, or own MPointCloud.

You may describe software you created that integrates with or uses MPointCloud, but you must distinguish your work from MPointCloud itself.

You may not:

- remove references identifying MPointCloud as a third-party component;
- replace MPointCloud authorship or ownership notices with your own;
- claim copyright over MPointCloud;
- claim ownership of MPointCloud;
- present MPointCloud as an internally developed library when it was obtained under this License;
- register or assert intellectual-property rights over MPointCloud or substantially identical implementations derived from it.

Integration of MPointCloud into another product does not create joint ownership or derivative ownership of MPointCloud.

## 6. Redistribution

You may redistribute unmodified compiled MPointCloud binaries when they are reasonably necessary for operation of a product, library, service, package, or application that uses MPointCloud.

Redistribution must preserve this License or provide a clear reference to where this License can be obtained.

You may not redistribute MPointCloud as:

- a standalone commercial library;
- a rebranded library;
- a competing PCD library presented as your own product;
- a modified binary that falsely retains the MPointCloud name;
- part of a software-development kit whose primary purpose is to resell or repackage MPointCloud itself without written permission.

Bundling MPointCloud with a broader application, engineering tool, visualization system, plugin, game, service, package, or other substantial software product is permitted.

## 7. NuGet and Package-Manager Distribution

MPointCloud may be distributed through NuGet and other software package-management or dependency-management systems authorized by Mekneo.

Users may:

- install MPointCloud from an authorized package source;
- reference MPointCloud from a .NET project;
- declare MPointCloud as a package dependency;
- publish their own packages that depend upon MPointCloud;
- include MPointCloud as a transitive dependency;
- restore MPointCloud automatically through standard package-management tooling;
- distribute applications that include MPointCloud binaries as a result of normal build, publish, deployment, or packaging processes.

A package that depends upon MPointCloud is not considered a prohibited redistribution merely because MPointCloud is restored or delivered transitively through a dependency graph.

A compiled application may also contain MPointCloud through standard .NET publishing mechanisms, including deployment models that copy, bundle, package, or otherwise include dependency binaries with the application.

This permission does not allow a third party to:

- publish an unofficial package whose primary content is a copy of MPointCloud;
- mirror or republish the official MPointCloud package under another package identifier without permission;
- modify MPointCloud and distribute the modified binary as an official or compatible MPointCloud release;
- remove Mekneo attribution or licensing information;
- represent an unofficial package as being published, supported, or endorsed by Mekneo.

Official MPointCloud package identifiers, feeds, and distribution channels may be designated by Mekneo.

Where technically practical, packages that directly depend on MPointCloud should preserve package metadata identifying MPointCloud as a dependency.

## 8. Reverse Engineering and Modification

Except where applicable law expressly prohibits such restrictions, you may not:

- reverse engineer;
