This restriction does not prohibit users from independently implementing the publicly documented PCD file format.

## 8A. Public Sample Code Permission

Public sample source code distributed by Mekneo specifically to demonstrate use of the documented MPointCloud API may be copied, modified, adapted, incorporated into, and redistributed as part of applications or other software that uses MPointCloud.

This sample-code permission exists so developers can use the examples as practical starting points without exposing or licensing the proprietary MPointCloud implementation source.

When sample code is substantially copied into your own application, you may place the resulting application code under your own project license and are not required to preserve the MPointCloud sample file header inside adapted snippets.

If a Mekneo sample is redistributed substantially unchanged as a standalone example or tutorial, its existing Mekneo attribution and this sample-code permission should be preserved.

This permission applies only to source files clearly distributed as public samples. It does not apply to:

- MPointCloud library implementation source;
- internal tests;
- benchmarks;
- fixture generators;
- internal tooling;
- proprietary development utilities;
- source code obtained through unauthorized disclosure, reverse engineering, or decompilation.

The MPointCloud binary used by the sample remains governed by the other terms of this License.

## 9. Interfaces and Interoperability

The public API surface of MPointCloud may be used by external applications, plugins, engines, tools, converters, packages, and other software.

Users may create their own software that interoperates with MPointCloud through its documented public APIs.

Nothing in this License grants ownership of those APIs, their implementation, internal architecture, or documentation.

## 10. PCD and Point Cloud Library Attribution

MPointCloud is an independent .NET implementation of the publicly documented PCD (Point Cloud Data) file format.

The PCD format and the Point Cloud Library (PCL) project are not owned by MPointCloud or Mekneo.

MPointCloud does not claim ownership of:

- the PCD file-format specification;
- the Point Cloud Library project;
- PCL source code;
- PCL documentation;
- third-party standards or specifications used for interoperability.

MPointCloud is not an official component of PCL and is not affiliated with, sponsored by, or endorsed by the Point Cloud Library project unless expressly stated otherwise.

The MPointCloud implementation, including its .NET code, architecture, performance optimizations, APIs, tests, tooling, integration layers, documentation, packaging, and other original material, remains the intellectual property of Mekneo.

## 11. Independent Implementations

Nothing in this License prevents another party from independently creating its own implementation of the PCD file format based solely on publicly available specifications and documentation.

However, this License does not permit copying, reproducing, adapting, translating, reverse engineering, or deriving such an implementation from MPointCloud source code or proprietary internal implementation details.

